# MIXED MARTIAL ARTS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Mixed Martial Arts (MMA).

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the complete performance profile of MMA athletes and to individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Mixed Martial Arts is a full-contact combat sport integrating striking, wrestling and submission grappling within a unified ruleset.

Success depends upon:

Adaptability.

Technical versatility.

Decision making.

Physical preparation.

Recovery.

The athlete must perform efficiently across every combat range.

---

# Philosophy

MMA is the most complete combat sport.

No single discipline is sufficient.

The athlete must continuously integrate striking, wrestling and grappling while adapting to rapidly changing situations.

The objective is not to master isolated techniques.

The objective is to solve continuously evolving combat problems.

