# Final Principle

Mixed Martial Arts is not the sum of multiple combat sports.

It is a unique combat system requiring continuous adaptation across striking,

clinch,

wrestling,

and ground fighting.

The athlete who transitions seamlessly between every phase of combat,

while maintaining physical efficiency and tactical intelligence,

creates the greatest probability of victory.